1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:05,450
It always runs out on a Saturday.
Weekly limit reached. Resets Sunday at 2:00 PM, about 33 hours from now.

2
00:00:05,450 --> 00:00:09,300
Where did your week go?
ToBeBestMe, a mod that runs inside Claude Code itself, answers that.

3
00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:20,750
Every day, stacked by the project that used it. 82% of the weekly limit so far, across 6 projects.

4
00:00:20,750 --> 00:00:26,900
storefront did more than half of it. It used 49% of this week’s limit.

5
00:00:26,900 --> 00:00:32,900
Know before you run out.
At this pace it runs out Saturday at 5:21 AM, about 33 hours before it resets.

6
00:00:32,900 --> 00:00:37,550
Know before you run out.
Ease off to a quarter of today’s pace, and it lasts the week.

7
00:00:37,550 --> 00:00:46,200
The chat that needs you most comes first, as the lead card. The rest of the waiting chats follow, from every project. The pane counts 4 more waiting.

8
00:00:46,200 --> 00:00:53,350
One line, always in view.
Context and limits above where you type. Amber when one runs low, red when it’s nearly gone.

9
00:00:53,350 --> 00:01:00,800
See what a change would buy back. Half the Opus work on Sonnet moves the run-out from 5:21 AM to 1:15 PM: 7 h 54 min more.

10
00:01:00,800 --> 00:01:05,800
Fix it in the pane, not in the chat.
The pane works out the change itself and shows what’s there now, and what it becomes after.

11
00:01:05,800 --> 00:01:10,450
Fix it in the pane, not in the chat.
Nothing is written until you press Save change. Nothing goes through the conversation.

12
00:01:10,450 --> 00:01:20,100
All of it, in one pane beside the chat.
The week, the chat that needs you, savings and fixes, beside your chat.

13
00:01:20,100 --> 00:01:27,800
See where your week went.
/plugin install tobebestme --marketplace vradulthub-cloud/tobebestme
